# Initial SSH public keys for the base login (vm.ssh_user, "rocky").
# One OpenSSH public key per line, authorized_keys format. Blank lines
# and comments are ignored. The generator merges these with
# vm.ssh_public_key / vm.ssh_public_key_file into the instance's
# ssh-keys metadata.
#
# This is the committed example. The generator reads the local copy at
# config/rocky_authorized_keys, which is gitignored:
#     cp config/examples/rocky_authorized_keys config/rocky_authorized_keys
# Add your keys to the copy. Public keys are safe to share, but the
# local copy stays out of git; never put private keys anywhere in here.
#
# Example:
# ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA... user@host
